{% doc %}
  Renders a product card (Figma collection grid): a rounded tile with the product image on top, badges
  on the image, then the full title, an optional subtitle and the price.

  Badges (top-left of the image):
  - "Sold out" when no variant can be bought, otherwise "Sale" when the compare-at price is higher.
  - Merchant badges from the product metafield custom.badges ("Badges"): a list of references to
    "Badge" metaobject entries (Content > Metaobjects > Badges). Each entry has a Label and its own
    Background colour and Text colour, so "New" can be cream and "Bestseller" red. One field, so the
    merchant always sets badges the same way, and it can become a clean "Badges" filter (M5).
  Badge colours: an entry's own colours; without them, the default badge colour scheme. Sale and
  Sold out use their own colour schemes (Theme settings > Product cards).
  Subtitle: the product metafield custom.subtitle ("Subtitle", single line text), shown only when
  filled, e.g. "Eau de Parfum · 50ml".
  Both fields are defined once in the admin (Settings > Custom data > Products); see the M3.7 notes.

  The whole card is one link (the title's link stretches over the card), so keyboard users meet one
  stop per product and screen readers hear the product name once.

  Without a product (e.g. a section in the theme editor with no collection chosen yet) it renders a
  placeholder card, so the layout still looks right.

  Tile style (style: 'tile', Figma collection page, M5.2): the photo fills the whole card and the info
  sits on a white strip over its bottom edge. The tile takes the size its parent gives it (a bento grid
  area, or an aspect ratio set by the parent), so it has no image ratio of its own. With show_details,
  hovering the tile (or tabbing into it) slides the strip up to show more:
  - the rating, from Shopify's standard review fields reviews.rating / reviews.rating_count. Review apps
    (Judge.me, Okendo...) fill these; Shopify has no ratings of its own. Hidden when empty.
  - the first words of the product description
  - the quick add button (snippets/quick-add.liquid) and a "View details" label
  Phones and tablets (no hover) keep the short strip: a tap opens the product.

  @param {product} [product] - The product. Leave empty for a placeholder card
  @param {string} [style] - 'card' (default: image on top, info below) or 'tile' (see above)
  @param {string} [image_ratio] - Card style: 'portrait' (4:5, default), 'square', 'landscape' (4:3) or 'original'
  @param {string} [sizes] - The image's sizes attribute. Default: 4 per row on desktop, 2 on phones
  @param {string} [loading] - 'eager' or 'lazy' to override the image snippet's automatic choice
  @param {boolean} [show_secondary_image] - Show the second product image on hover (default false)
  @param {string} [heading_tag] - Tag for the title, default 'h3'
  @param {boolean} [show_details] - Tile style: reveal the details panel on hover / keyboard focus
  @param {boolean} [show_rating] - Details panel: show the review rating when an app provides one
  @param {boolean} [show_description] - Details panel: show the start of the description
  @param {string} [cart_options] - Details panel quick add, products with several variants: 'add_first' or 'link'

  @example
  {% render 'product-card', product: product %}
  {% render 'product-card', product: product, image_ratio: 'square', show_secondary_image: true %}
  {% render 'product-card', product: product, style: 'tile', show_details: true, show_rating: true, show_description: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign card_style = style | default: 'card'
  assign ratio = image_ratio | default: 'portrait'
  assign image_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 990px) 25vw, 50vw'
  assign title_tag = heading_tag | default: 'h3'

  assign image_class = ''
  if ratio != 'original'
    assign image_class = 'image--cover'
  endif

  # A tile always fills its box: the photo is cropped to the tile's shape
  assign media_class = 'product-card__media--' | append: ratio
  if card_style == 'tile'
    assign image_class = 'image--cover'
    assign media_class = 'product-card__media--fill'
  endif
-%}

{%- if product != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    # Second image for the hover swap: only when asked for and the product has one
    assign secondary_image = nil
    if show_secondary_image and product.media.size > 1
      assign secondary_image = product.media[1].preview_image
    endif

    assign on_sale = false
    if product.compare_at_price > product.price
      assign on_sale = true
    endif
  -%}
  <div class="product-card product-card--{{ card_style }}{% if secondary_image %} product-card--has-secondary{% endif %}">
    <div class="product-card__media {{ media_class }}">
      {%- liquid
        # The image is decorative here (alt=""): the title link right below names the product, so a
        # screen reader would otherwise hear the name twice.
        render 'image', image: product.featured_media.preview_image, class: image_class, sizes: image_sizes, alt: '', loading: loading
        if secondary_image
          render 'image', image: secondary_image, class: 'image--cover product-card__secondary', sizes: image_sizes, alt: '', loading: 'lazy'
        endif
      -%}

      <div class="product-card__badges">
        {%- if product.available == false -%}
          <span class="product-card__badge color-{{ settings.sold_out_badge_color_scheme.id }}">{{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}</span>
        {%- elsif on_sale -%}
          <span class="product-card__badge color-{{ settings.sale_badge_color_scheme.id }}">{{ 'products.badge.sale' | t }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The product's "Badges" field (custom.badges). Usually a list (.value is an array), but a single
          value (one metaobject or one text) is handled too, so a badge never silently disappears.
          snippets/product-badge.liquid draws one badge: own colours for a Badge metaobject entry,
          otherwise the default badge colour scheme.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign badges_field = product.metafields.custom.badges -%}
        {%- if badges_field != blank -%}
          {%- assign badges_value = badges_field.value -%}
          {%- if badges_field.type contains 'list.' -%}
            {%- for badge in badges_value -%}
              {% render 'product-badge', badge: badge %}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {% render 'product-badge', badge: badges_value %}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="product-card__panel">
      <div class="product-card__info">
        <div class="product-card__text">
          <{{ title_tag }} class="product-card__title">
            <a class="product-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
          </{{ title_tag }}>
          {%- assign subtitle = product.metafields.custom.subtitle.value -%}
          {%- if subtitle != blank -%}
            <p class="product-card__subtitle">{{ subtitle | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {% render 'price', product: product %}
      </div>

      {%- if card_style == 'tile' and show_details -%}
        {%- liquid
          # Rating: Shopify's standard review fields, filled by a review app. .value of a rating field
          # is a rating object: .rating (e.g. 4.9) and .scale_max (e.g. 5).
          assign rating = nil
          if show_rating
            assign rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
            assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | default: 0
            # scale_max is stored as "5.0": round it so screen readers hear "out of 5"
            assign rating_max = rating.scale_max | round
          endif

          assign description = ''
          if show_description
            assign description = product.description | strip_html | strip_newlines | truncatewords: 16
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="product-card__details">
          <div class="product-card__details-inner">
            {%- if rating != blank -%}
              <p class="product-card__rating">
                <span class="product-card__stars" aria-hidden="true">
                  {{- rating.rating | round: 1 }} <span class="product-card__star">★</span>
                </span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">
                  {{- 'products.card.rating' | t: rating: rating.rating, max: rating_max -}}
                </span>
                {%- if rating_count > 0 -%}
                  <span class="product-card__reviews">{{ 'products.card.reviews_count' | t: count: rating_count }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if description != blank -%}
              <p class="product-card__description">{{ description }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Above the stretched link (z-index), so the cart button gets the click. "View details" is a
              label only: the whole tile is already the link to the product.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="product-card__actions">
              {% render 'quick-add', product: product, size: 44, icon_color: '#7d0000', options: cart_options %}
              <span class="product-card__more" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="product-card__more-label">{{ 'products.card.view_details' | t }}</span>
                {{- 'icon-arrow.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  {%- comment -%} Placeholder card: same layout, sample content, no link {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="product-card product-card--{{ card_style }} product-card--placeholder">
    <div class="product-card__media {{ media_class }}">
      {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'product-card__placeholder' }}
    </div>
    <div class="product-card__panel">
      <div class="product-card__info">
        <div class="product-card__text">
          <{{ title_tag }} class="product-card__title">{{ 'products.card.placeholder_title' | t }}</{{ title_tag }}>
        </div>
        <div class="price"><span class="price__current">{{ 2100 | money }}</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    Figma card: a white glass tile, small rounded corners (19px), soft shadow; image on top, then the
    title + subtitle on the left and the red price on the right.
  */
  .product-card {
    position: relative; /* the title link's ::after stretches over the whole card */
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-card-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--color-glass-strong);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-frost));
    backdrop-filter: blur(var(--glass-frost));
  }

  /* Keyboard focus: the ring goes around the whole card, not just the title text */
  .product-card:has(.product-card__link:focus-visible) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .product-card__link:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
  }

  .product-card__media {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .product-card__media--portrait {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
  }

  .product-card__media--square {
    aspect-ratio: 1;
  }

  .product-card__media--landscape {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
  }

  .product-card__media .image > img {
    transition:
      transform var(--duration-slow) var(--ease-out),
      opacity var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  /* Hover: a slow, gentle zoom; with a second image, that one fades in on top */
  .product-card:hover .product-card__media .image > img {
    transform: scale(1.04);
  }

  .product-card__secondary {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
  }

  .product-card__secondary > img {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .product-card--has-secondary:hover .product-card__secondary > img {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .product-card__media .image > img {
      transition: none;
    }

    .product-card:hover .product-card__media .image > img {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .product-card__placeholder {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: 100%;
    background-color: var(--color-tint-subtle);
    fill: var(--color-tint-border);
  }

  /*
    Badges top-left of the image. Figma: a cream rounded rectangle with red text ("New").
    Colours come from the colour scheme chosen in Theme settings > Product cards: the scheme class
    (color-scheme-N) paints the scheme's background; the text uses the scheme's accent.
  */
  .product-card__badges {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: var(--space-sm);
    inset-inline-start: var(--space-sm);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .product-card__badge {
    padding: 0.3em 0.75em;
    border-radius: 0.75em;
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  /*
    Two classes on purpose: the scheme class sets color: var(--color-text) with one class, and which
    stylesheet loads last isn't guaranteed. Two classes always win, so the text is the scheme's accent.
  */
  .product-card .product-card__badge {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* A badge entry with its own colours (Content > Metaobjects > Badges); three classes beat the rule above */
  .product-card .product-card__badge.product-card__badge--own-colors {
    background-color: var(--badge-bg);
    color: var(--badge-fg);
  }

  /* Title + subtitle left, price right; the price drops below on a narrow card */
  .product-card__info {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
  }

  .product-card__text {
    flex: 1 1 10rem;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .product-card__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .product-card__link {
    color: var(--color-text);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  /* The stretched link: an invisible box over the whole card, so a click anywhere opens the product */
  .product-card__link::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .product-card__subtitle {
    margin: var(--space-2xs) 0 0;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 70%, var(--color-background));
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
  }

  .product-card .price {
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-sm);
  }

  /*
    ---------- Tile style (Figma collection page) ----------
    A white tile with a 4px frame; the photo fills it and the white info strip sits over the photo's
    bottom edge. The tile fills the box its parent gives it (block-size: 100%).
    Layers: isolation makes the tile its own stacking context, so the photo can sit at z-index -1
    (under the strip) while the stretched title link (z-index 1) still covers the whole tile, and the
    cart button (z-index 2) sits above that.
    container-type: size lets short tiles drop the description (container query below).
  */
  .product-card--tile {
    isolation: isolate;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    block-size: 100%;
    padding: 0.25rem;
    border: 0;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 0 5px 25px 0 #0000000d; /* Figma collection-card shadow */
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
    backdrop-filter: none;
    container-type: size;
  }

  .product-card__media--fill {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0.25rem;
    z-index: -1;
    border-radius: calc(var(--radius-sm) - 0.25rem);
  }

  .product-card__media--fill > .image {
    block-size: 100%;
  }

  /* Badges a little further in, like the Figma ("Trending" sits ~24px from the corner) */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__badges {
    inset-block-start: var(--space-lg);
    inset-inline-start: var(--space-lg);
  }

  /*
    The details strip is glass over the photo (Figma Glass: Light -45deg 80%, Frost 157.25; drop shadow
    0 0 14.77px #000000 5%).
    - Light -45deg = the light comes from the top LEFT: a bright 1px rim on the top and left edges (80%
      white) and a weaker one bottom-right.
    - Frost: the theme maps Frost 100 to a 35px blur, so 157.25 = 35px x 1.5725 = 55px.
    - The fill is the theme's strong glass (50% white), so the text stays readable on any photo.
    Figma's Refraction, Depth, Dispersion and Splay bend light through the glass; CSS has no equivalent,
    so the blur, rim and shadow carry the effect.
  */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__panel {
    border-radius: calc(var(--radius-sm) - 0.25rem);
    background-color: var(--color-glass-strong);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 14.77px 0 #0000000d,
      inset 1px 1px 0 #ffffffcc,
      inset -1px -1px 0 #ffffff80;
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(55px);
    backdrop-filter: blur(55px);
  }

  /* Strip: title + subtitle left, price right and vertically centred (Figma: ~103px tall at 1920px) */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
  }

  /*
    The glass blur (backdrop-filter) makes the strip the box that absolutely positioned children measure
    from, so the title link's click area (::after, inset: 0) would only cover the strip. The tile is a
    size container, so 100cqh = the tile's full height: the click area hangs from the strip's bottom
    edge and reaches the top of the tile again (-0.25rem = the tile's white frame).
  */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__link::after {
    inset: auto -0.25rem -0.25rem;
    block-size: 100cqh;
  }

  .product-card--tile .product-card__title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  /*
    Price on the right edge. The price lines are stacked in a column, right-aligned: as a wrapping row,
    the unit price line (flex-basis 100%) made the box as wide as both lines side by side, so the price
    started mid-card and squeezed the title.
  */
  .product-card--tile .price {
    flex: 0 1 auto;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-end;
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    font-size: var(--font-size-body-lg);
    text-align: end;
  }

  .product-card--tile .price__unit {
    flex-basis: auto;
  }

  .product-card--tile .price__current {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /*
    Details panel: folded away (0fr) until the tile is hovered or something inside has keyboard focus,
    then it grows to its natural height (1fr) and the strip slides up over the photo. visibility keeps
    the folded content away from screen readers and the Tab key; tabbing onto the title link opens the
    panel first (focus-within), so the cart button is visible before it gets focus.
  */
  .product-card__details {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: 0fr;
    transition: grid-template-rows var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .product-card__details-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    min-block-size: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-inline: var(--space-lg);
    visibility: hidden;
    transition: visibility 0s linear var(--duration-base);
  }

  .product-card--tile:focus-within .product-card__details {
    grid-template-rows: 1fr;
  }

  .product-card--tile:focus-within .product-card__details-inner {
    visibility: visible;
    transition-delay: 0s;
  }

  /* Hover only where there is a real pointer: on touch screens a tap goes straight to the product */
  @media (hover: hover) {
    .product-card--tile:hover .product-card__details {
      grid-template-rows: 1fr;
    }

    .product-card--tile:hover .product-card__details-inner {
      visibility: visible;
      transition-delay: 0s;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .product-card__details {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  /* "4.9 ★  213 reviews": number + gold star, then the count in a soft pill */
  .product-card__rating {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
  }

  .product-card__star {
    color: #c8a24b;
  }

  .product-card__reviews {
    padding: 0.15em 0.6em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: var(--color-tint-subtle);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .product-card__description {
    display: -webkit-box;
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text) 70%, var(--color-background));
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    line-clamp: 2;
  }

  .product-card__actions {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2; /* above the stretched title link */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-md);
  }

  /*
    The glass cart button needs something behind it to show; on the white strip it gets a soft tint
    instead (three classes beat quick-add's own two-class rule).
  */
  .product-card__actions .quick-add .quick-add__button {
    background-color: var(--color-tint);
  }

  /* "View details": a label in the Figma pill style; the whole tile is the link */
  .product-card__more {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    block-size: 2.5rem;
    padding-inline: var(--space-lg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-background);
    font-size: var(--font-size-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    pointer-events: none; /* clicks fall through to the stretched link */
  }

  .product-card__more svg {
    display: none;
    inline-size: 1rem;
    block-size: 1rem;
  }

  /* Tiles: the subtitle is always one line ("…"), so the strip keeps the same height */
  .product-card--tile .product-card__subtitle {
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Short tiles (e.g. 1280px screens, the shortest bento tiles): no description, so the panel fits */
  @container (max-height: 24rem) {
    .product-card__description {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /*
    Very short tiles (the bento's 1-column tiles on 1200-1440px screens are ~190-220px tall): a compact
    strip, one line each for title and price, no subtitle, so the photo still shows (~1/3 strip, as in the
    Figma at 1920px).
  */
  @container (max-height: 16rem) {
    .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
      padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md);
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__title {
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__subtitle {
      display: none;
    }

    .product-card--tile .price {
      font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    }

    .product-card--tile .price__unit {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  /*
    Narrow tiles, measured on the tile itself (a size container), so it works wherever the card sits.
    - Up to 24rem (phones, small bento tiles): "View details" becomes a round arrow button; the label
      wrapped onto two lines here.
    - Up to 20rem (the 1-column bento tiles on small laptops): the price goes under the title instead of
      beside it, so the title gets the full width and words never break letter by letter.
  */
  @container (max-width: 24rem) {
    .product-card__more {
      justify-content: center;
      inline-size: 2.75rem;
      block-size: 2.75rem;
      padding: 0;
    }

    .product-card__more-label {
      display: none;
    }

    .product-card__more svg {
      display: block;
    }
  }

  @container (max-width: 20rem) {
    .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: flex-start;
      row-gap: var(--space-2xs);
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__text {
      flex: 1 1 100%;
    }

    .product-card--tile .price {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--space-xs);
      margin-inline-start: 0;
      font-size: var(--font-size-body);
      text-align: start;
    }
  }

  /*
    Phones (one tile per row): a slimmer strip, so the photo keeps most of the tile. Title up to 2 lines,
    price at body size; the text column gets the room and never breaks mid-word.
  */
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .product-card--tile .product-card__info {
      gap: var(--space-sm);
      padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__text {
      flex: 1 1 auto;
    }

    .product-card--tile .product-card__title {
      display: -webkit-box;
      overflow: hidden;
      -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
      -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
      line-clamp: 2;
    }

    .product-card--tile .price {
      flex: none;
      font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
